description:
Design a clock buffer driver that generates a series of output clock signals based on a single input clock. With a parameterized width `n`, it shifts the buffered clock signals on each rising edge of the input clock, maintaining a circular buffer effect. The output `clk_out` will present a delayed version of the input clock, producing `n` clock signals that are synchronized but phase-shifted with respect to each other.
module top_module(
  input clk,
  output [n-1:0] clk_out
);

code:
module top_module(
  input clk,
  output [n-1:0] clk_out
);parameter n = 4; // number of output clock signals

reg [n-1:0] clk_buf;

always @(posedge clk) begin
  clk_buf <= {clk_buf[n-2:0], clk_buf[n-1]};
end

assign clk_out = clk_buf;

endmodule

