description:
Design a ring oscillator that generates a clock signal and its complementary output using a series of inverters. The module consists of a configurable number of inverters, specified by the parameter n, each introducing a defined propagation delay. The output of the last inverter is internally connected back to the input of the first inverter, creating a feedback loop that oscillates continuously. The resulting clock signal (clk) toggles based on the state of the first inverter while its complement (clk_bar) is derived directly from it.
module top_module(
  output reg clk,
  output reg clk_bar
);

code:
module top_module(
  output reg clk,
  output reg clk_bar
);parameter n = 5; // number of inverters
parameter delay = 10; // delay through each inverter in ps

// Verilog code for the ring oscillator goes here
genvar i;
wire [n-1:0] nodes;

// Generate inverters
generate
  for (i = 0; i < n; i = i + 1) begin : inv_gen
    not #(delay) inv (nodes[i], nodes[i-1]);
  end
endgenerate

// Connect the last inverter output to the first inverter input
assign nodes[n-1] = nodes[0];

// Generate clock signal and its complement
always @(nodes[0]) begin
  clk <= nodes[0];
  clk_bar <= ~nodes[0];
end

endmodule

